course: dictionary
lesson: 6094
title: When a name becomes a word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words start as names. Methuselah is a man in the Bible who was said to have lived 969 years, so people use his name to mean very old. If someone says, «You are as old as Methuselah!» they mean you are extremely old, not that you are really his age.
explain: «Bristlecone pines grow very slowly in harsh mountain places and can live for nearly five thousand years; one called Methuselah is over four thousand years old.» Here Methuselah is the name of a tree. The clues are grow very slowly, can live for nearly five thousand years, and over four thousand years old. They all show the tree is very old.
explain: Always check the whole sentence, because one word can have more than one meaning. A methuselah can also be a very large wine bottle. Swap your meaning into the sentence to test it: «One very old tree is over four thousand years old» still makes sense, so the meaning fits.
fact: Methuselah is a man in the Book of Genesis in the Bible, said to have lived 969 years.
fact: «Methuselah» can mean a very old person or thing, in informal use.
fact: «As old as Methuselah» means extremely old.
fact: A methuselah is also a very large wine bottle holding six litres.
fact: One bristlecone pine in the White Mountains of California is named Methuselah, and it is over 4,800 years old.
exercise: «One bristlecone pine called Methuselah is over four thousand years old.» What does Methuselah mean here? | A very large wine bottle | A man who lived 969 years | A mountain in California | *A very old tree
exercise: The Bible says Methuselah lived 969 years. Who or what was Methuselah in the Bible? | A pine tree in California | *A man said to have lived 969 years | A mountain in the White Mountains | A wine bottle
exercise: Grandma says, «That old chair is as old as Methuselah!» What does she mean? | *It is extremely old | It is made of wine | It is brand new | It is a tree in California
test: At a party, a bottle labelled methuselah stands on the table. What is it most likely to be? | A very old man | A tiny sweet | A bristlecone pine | *A very large wine bottle holding six litres
test: Which clue shows that the tree called Methuselah is very old? | Grow very slowly | Pines | Harsh mountain places | *Over four thousand years old
exam: In «as old as Methuselah», what does the name help us say? | *Extremely old | Extremely wet | Extremely loud | Extremely tall
